Z||000000||Richard Parnell||11-03-2001||10:39 AM||||My radiator fan quit working (again).  The first time it was burned out.  The next time it was the fuse.  This time the fuse seems ok.  Is there a fusable link somewhere that I don't know about.  If the fan is burned out, is there a better replacement fan that can be used? It catches me by surprise each time.  Like when I get off the freeway and into downtown traffic.  I hope I didn't damage the engine.  All the water steamed out before I realized what was going on.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Richard Parnell||11-03-2001||11:43 AM||||Forgot to add: the fan runs all the time.  It has since I got the car.  Someone probably bypassed whatever shutoff switch there is but I have no idea where. Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||11-03-2001||12:12 PM||||The cheap haynes book has all the fan wiring in it.<P>It's also here<A HREF="http://www.euronet.nl/users/fo_elmo/fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>Fiero-Tech-Zone</A><P>On with key would be a short or intentional change to the control line. Unless you have the AC on all the time in what case there may be nothing wrong there.<P>You can check for main power easy enough at the relay... the heavy Red?(It's one of the heavy ones...) lead is hot at all times.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">   <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 11-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Richard Parnell||11-03-2001||04:14 PM||||Ogre where is the relay you mentioned.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Richard Parnell||11-03-2001||04:53 PM||||Ogre- another question.  The wiring diagram shows a fusable link in the circuit.  Where would that be located?  Also when I turn on the ignition normally, the fan comes on immediately.  Now when I turn on the ignition and measure for voltage in the plug going to the fan, I see no voltage.  As I said the fuse for then fan is good.||||reg||5
Z||000005||rogergarrison||11-03-2001||05:34 PM||||i dont know for sure, but most or all the fusible links in mine are near the battery.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Richard Parnell||11-03-2001||07:00 PM||||Now get this!  When I measure the voltage from any fuse in the fuse box I read 12v. But when I measure the voltage from either the radiator fan fuse or the AC fan fuse I get no voltage.  Something somewhere is open.<BR>Help!!!||||reg||5
Z||000007||FieroBUZZ||11-03-2001||09:07 PM||||The relay for the fan is on the wall just ahead of the driver's side headlight. I believe all the fusible links are near the battery.<BR>The red wire (one of two big ones) should be hot at all times.  If you join the 2 large outer wires, the fan should run.  If these are okay, then the fan works, and the fuse/fusible link are good.  The relay itself may be bad.  When the temp sensor reads hot, it grounds the circuit and the fan starts.  <P>If I read right, then when you turn your key to on, the fan DOES run.  If the A/C is off then the relay may be stuck or the fan may be 'hotwired' to always be on.  Sorry if this doesn't help.<P>Gary||||reg||1
Z||000008||FieroSoul||11-04-2001||08:17 AM||||  There is more than one fan used. Which one do you have?  The 2-speed heavy duty has a relay attached to the fan shroud and is very different from the standard fan.  Also very expensive. $200+ as opposed to about $30. <BR>  I speak from experience. I bought a used one from Kick Hill when mine quit.  One of the magnets broke loose and chewed through the windings in a couple of places. That will cause them to stop!||||reg||1
Z||000009||Richard Parnell||11-05-2001||11:52 AM||||An odd thing happened that tells me that the problem is in the ignition switch or something in the steering column.  I got in the car leaned over to the passenger side to roll down the window.  While doing this I held on to the steering wheel.  The blower for the heater came on for a few seconds.  But this was without the key in the ignition.  This is too weird.  I'm feeling like I'll have to rewire everything.  Please read the other topic about status of problem if you think you have any other ideas let me know. Thanks all. ||||reg||1
